# Git LFS
#
# Only the expression matrices need LFS: shared/bulk_expression.parquet is
# 137 MB, above GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit, so a normal push of it is
# rejected outright. Tracking the whole *.parquet pattern keeps the 12 matrices
# consistent with each other (239 MB total, well inside the 1 GB free quota).
#
# The .npy arrays are deliberately NOT in LFS. There are 4,481 of them averaging
# ~31 KB, and the largest is 8.5 MB -- far below any git limit. Pushing them as
# 4,481 separate LFS objects would be slower, would burn the LFS object budget,
# and would force every cloner to install git-lfs to get files plain git handles
# perfectly well.
*.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Treat saved model weights and arrays as binary so git never tries to diff or
# line-ending-convert them.
*.npy binary
*.pt  binary
*.gz  binary
*.RCC binary
